core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T08:17:11-07:00","id":1532504,"title":"","content":"a big congratulations to you and the rest of the team!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T10:09:44-07:00","id":1532511,"title":"","content":"Lovely, cant wait to read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T15:28:24-07:00","id":1532670,"title":"","content":"How did I not know we were finally getting Hedge Sorcery? That\u2019s been <i>the</i> thing I\u2019ve always been grumpy about Changeling missing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T16:02:19-07:00","id":1532673,"title":"","content":"I've got it, and I'm excited to flesh out my own chronicle setting. Definitely going to give the BriarNet a closer look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T20:49:01-07:00","id":1532884,"title":"","content":"I like the Groves quite a bit. Giving more mechanical definition to the Hedge is important, and I like how each location gives bonuses/penalties to various ways of interacting with it. The section on Goblin Queens is really neat, and the section on how other Splats interact with the Hedge was really good. Of COURSE dropping a monster that can go into a raging frenzy into a psychoactive landscape will cause big splashes.<br /> <br /> Coneironautics just screams Inception, when Oneiromancy was already pure Inception haha. I definitely support having a bestiary of basic Eidolon archetypes, it's so much easier to use than having to stat up on the fly. Big fan of Awakened Mages having Awakened Eidolons as well.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of good stuff in here concerning expansions on already existing systems, but I can't lie that Hedge Sorcery is really... barebones? There really isn't a guide to making your own rituals beyond &quot;Bigger effect=More doors&quot; which straight up doesn't work when you have so few examples of what rituals looks like to give a guide of how big an effect is compared to how many doors it should take. I'm glad it's in the game, but it feels like something is missing.<br /> <br /> Limens are such a good idea and are worth building a whole campaign around, but there's so little in terms of game mechanics to support them. There's no mention of a natural Limen's Fortification rating, there's no mechanical guidance behind the progression of Stage 1 to Stage 2 or 3, and there's no guidance as to the spatial limits of the Limens, which is an issue when they spread so rapidly. A turn in CoD being 6 Seconds, 1 Yard to .5 Miles per 6 seconds is extremely rapid and if you go by &quot;rules as written&quot; an unattended Limen will just swallow the entire planet. There's an incredible amount of mechanical guidance missing for Limens which makes them feel more like an &quot;Inspirational concept&quot; for Storytellers instead of usable gameplay elements. Feels very First Drafty which is a shame given we're not gonna get any follow-ups.<br /> <br /> Congratulations to Changeling for now having 6 distinct types of non-human NPCs and therefore(as always) the most. Dreamborn and Geasa are neat. Dreamborn particularly just scream that one episode of Star Trek when holo-Moriarty gains sentience because he was programmed to be too smart. They also give me weird uncomfortable(but fun uncomfortable) feelings about the fact that Eidolons are technically part of a person's subconscious thoughts and when one becomes Dreamborn that part just kind of... walks off. Imagine if a Mage's Eidolon decided to walk off and establish its own wizardly practice in the dreaming roads. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26294-chris_john","name":"Chris_John","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T23:03:26-07:00","id":1533106,"title":"","content":"My big question: is there a preferred, official method to submit errata feedback, since there didn't seem to be anything on the store page or in the PDF spelling out to go to some form or other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28421-avigor","name":"avigor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T02:15:58-07:00","id":1533111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>avigor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1532501-the-hedge-is-on-dtrpg?p=1533106#post1533106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My big question: is there a preferred, official method to submit errata feedback, since there didn't seem to be anything on the store page or in the PDF spelling out to go to some form or other?</div> </div> </div> </div>The errata closed last week. The link was available during its first week available for sale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T19:18:27-07:00","id":1533146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1532501-the-hedge-is-on-dtrpg?p=1533111#post1533111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The errata closed last week. The link was available during its first week available for sale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disappointing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28421-avigor","name":"avigor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T20:44:56-07:00","id":1533152,"title":"","content":"Lots of stuff in here, including some nice lists of examples to build from.<br /> <br /> Good to see further expansions of the Hedge's big three sub-realms. Detailing the Hall of Mirrors is something I know people have been waiting for, and the restrictions on entry and egress are suitably unsettling. The BriarNet's content being split across three separate books (none of which are the corebook) is troublesome, but it's good to see that faerie e-commerce is as fraught with risks as attending Goblin Markets in-person. And, of course, the Dreaming Roads chapter delivers plenty of material to work out how it all fits together (including the all-important question of how one finds a specific dreamer).<br /> <br /> Dreamborn being in some ways analogous to the goetic beings of the same name from Beast is fun, as is their sharing motific terms with baubles. (It's a niche interaction that conceptually seems like it shouldn't work at all, but part of me wants to see what happens if someone uses Birth of the Dreamborn on the eidolon that represents an Empty changeling's bound token.) Shared Bastions coming back is a delight, as is its capacity to serve as a shortcut to the Roads if you don't mind minimizing the other benefit options available to you.<br /> <br /> The deeper look at goblin life is nice, particularly the applications of Goblin Credit and the material representations thereof, the limits of fair dealing, and the theory relating to what metaphysically happens to characters who become hobgoblins is fun for its relationship with goblin memory. The capacity for a Hedge Denizen to simply let their Icons wither because they simply no longer care about the person they used to be, while almost purely narrative fiat, is a solid tipping point to bear in mind for that transformation.<br /> <br /> The crossover bits are interesting, particularly given the odd edge cases they bring to bear: it's almost certainly unlikely for a werewolf pack to actually take a Huntsman as a totem, but there's enough connective tissue to link it back to old material about briarwolves accompanying the Fae on their hunts and werewolves being particularly susceptible to acclimation into different realms; mummies shortcutting past the lack of Twilight in the Hedge when they die is an entertainingly direct answer to that sort of question; and of course, Sin-Eaters being able to turn the right kind of Icons into Mementos is a cool point of thematic commonality between the two splats.<br /> <br /> The mechanical quality across the book as a whole is a little uneven, but it's definitely looking like it'll be handy for building out a game's setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T10:19:18-07:00","id":1533317,"title":"","content":"I haven't gotten a chance to finish, but the Hedge is one of my favorite settings and I am loving the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28417-fae_tail","name":"Fae_Tail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28417_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}